{:tier :glm-5.2, :verse 14, :comments ["<b>Eye to eye</b> — three times in the Masorah: אשר עין בעין נראה אתה ה' (here), כי עין בעין יראו בשוב ה' ציון (Isaiah 52:8), and the other: עין בעין שן בשן. In this world it is impossible to see the Shekhinah, as written: כי לא יראני האדם וחי — and this is what is written here: אשר עין בעין נראה, and adjacent to it: והמתה. But in the World to Come they will see and are destined to say: זה ה' קוינו לו. And likewise a hint to what they expounded: עין בעין — money, as written here: עין בעין, and adjacent to it: והמתה — meaning, if it were literally eye to eye, perhaps he would die. Therefore its meaning is: money."], :book :numbers, :voice :baal-haturim, :lang :en, :chapter 14, :notes {0 "The third Masorah occurrence 'עין בעין שן בשן' appears to be a phrase rather than a full verse citation; left unaddressed as it appears in the source. The reading of the final clause is somewhat compressed: the argument moves from the literal 'eye to eye' causing death, to the rabbinic reading that the phrase means monetary compensation."}, :source-witnesses [["On Your Way" "http://mobile.tora.ws/"]], :timestamp "2026-07-12T19:22:14.983138936Z", :translated-from :he, :model "glm-5.2"}